hey you do you like nature documentaries  and zelda then i have good news for you  if you're interested to see what it's  like to live as a pokablin and study  their behavior check out this video i  made recently  link in the description and the end card  so go check it out  [Music]  deciding what is canon and what isn't  isn't always  easy we know third party materials like  the cartoons cdi games and mangas  aren't canon since they were not made by  nintendo but then we have stuff like  creating a champion which also isn't  made by nintendo but it is an official  publication which is greenlit by the big  n  and even then some stuff in the book is  widely accepted to be canonical but we  also find  elements that have been retconned or  changed by age of calamity or left up to  the player to decide  like i said it isn't always  straightforward even the official  timeline has a footnote that states that  it's still  up to the player's imagination out of  all zelda games breath of the wild might  be the most divisive due to the  inclusion of so many additional content  stuff like the amiibos the dlc and not  to mention the freedom and open nature  of the game itself  it's one of the reasons why series  producer aj onuma has been reluctant to  say anything about the game's placement  in the zelda timeline  stating things like quote we revealed  where each zelda game fell on a timeline  and how their stories relate but we  didn't do that for breath the wild  we realized that people were enjoying  imagining the story that emerged from  the fragmentary imagery we were  providing  if we defined a restricted timeline then  there would be a definitive story and it  would eliminate the room for imagination  which wouldn't be as fun although this  might not be the answer a zelda lore  detective is looking  for i do understand the numerous  philosophy here after all breath of the  wild can be completed in so many ways  and depends on whether or not you got  all the memories completed all 120  shrines and how many divine beasts you  conquered  if any at all say i free every champion  from their divine beast  except for rivali because sweet revenge  for 100 years ago you arrogant oversized  drumstick  is that canon to my story probably not  and i think most people agree that the  quote-unquote true breath the wild story  is the one where link completes all the  main story missions since although the  game is  open-ended this is still the narrative  the game tries to push you towards this  includes getting the master sword all  your memories freeing the champions all  that good stuff  and then we have all the extra content  we'll talk about amiibo another time  since i feel like they deserve their own  separate video but when it comes to dlc  i think the story edition should  probably be considered canon  there's just too many important  revelations here to simply brush them  off as meaningless extras  examples of this being the trial of the  sword which sees link now with the fully  restored master sword and being able to  hear phi's voice within the sword  this is a pretty big deal and i'd argue  is too important not to be considered as  part of the main narrative  the same thing goes for the inclusion of  the fifth divine beast and the  introduction of monk boss koshia at the  end  as for the rest of the dlc well there's  a lot to take into consideration  some of which are obviously just nods  and references like rex's salvager  outfit from xenoblade and the nintendo  switch  shirt while others are nice expansions  to link's abilities such as the travel  medallion which i have no problems with  being considered canon  it's just another chica relic after all  and it doesn't stray away from what  should be possible in the game's story  which brings us to one piece of the dlc  which although has  all the characteristics of being nothing  more than a reference could actually be  canonical when we take a closer look at  it  i'm of course talking about the  treasures of misco the great bandit  oh hold on did i hear someone say bandit  oh hey mass nintendo bandit i didn't  know you were here even though i had to  animate this phone call in advance  but anyway what's up heard you were  talking about bandits and i thought  what better way to discuss a topic like  this than with yours truly  you know the masked nintendo bandit  can't argue with that  take it away will do sir the reason why  the misco treasure hunt found in dlc  pack 1  and 2 stands out from the other  collectibles is that it actually ties  into an already  established lore piece from the base  game the side quest that's fittingly  titled misco  the great bandit i'm pretty sure most  fans will be familiar with it since the  side quest itself is found inside the  dueling peak stable which is likely one  of the first places you encounter if you  follow king rome's directions and head  straight for kakariko right after  leaving the great plateau  you talk to these two guys grease some  palms and then they give you a riddle to  solve which leads to a treasure  allegedly belonging to this infamous  bandit  misco who this guy actually is or was is  actually something that we're going to  discuss further in  my part of the collab in this video  we're going to focus on the loot he  managed to acquire over the span of his  badass bandit career  we have the phantom armor midness helmet  korok mask and majora's mask in dlc pack  1  and the lobster shirt ravio's hood zanz  helmet  phantom ganon armor and royal guard  uniform in dlc pack 2.  obviously if we had to explain where  each and every one of them came from and  how they may have all transcended from  their respective games into  breath of the wild we would be here all  week they could all probably have an  entire theory video devoted to them  just trying to explain how and why but  the main point here is that although  they could be considered as  nods to the past and nothing more there  is actually very little standing in the  way of their inclusion being canonical  to the franchise  let's take the majoris mask for example  yes the evil entity known as  majora has left the mask by the end of  the game but the mask itself  still exists and was likely taken back  to hyrule by the happy mask salesman  when he departed termina since  well that's where he originated from in  the first place the mask has  obviously lost most of its power since  then and judging from the fact that the  moon isn't growing an angry face in  breath of the wild  it's safe to assume that this is still  the case after all these countless years  the same thing could be said about many  if not all the other artifacts that make  up misco's fortunes no matter how far  fetched there's always a way to explain  these relics still persisting to this  day  whether it's because they were never  completely destroyed or lost in the  first place or maybe it's a replica made  to remember  honor or memorialize a specific event or  individual who knows which is why the  backstory behind the misco dlc side  quest  does make sense canonically the relics  are described to have originally been in  the possession of the royal family of  hyrule before they were nabbed by misco  at some point in time  each and every one of these artifacts  has some degree of historical  significance so if anything  it would make less sense for the royal  family not to preserve them  similar to how in our own world we have  relics on this place some of which  hundreds of thousands of years old the  hylians may have been doing the same  thing  throughout history these ancient objects  could have been passed down from one  person to the next or replicated until  they ultimately land in the hands of  hyrule's leadership  yes even tingle's outfit can be  considered as such despite his  strange demeanor he did in fact aid the  various heroes of hyrule on multiple  occasions across the timeline  he is as much a historical figure as any  so in a sense hyrule castle housed a  museum of some kind a place where these  ancient relics from the distant past  were kept  but unlike a museum it is more likely  that these weren't open to the public  but only accessible to those close to  the royal family  very similar to the vaults of vatican  city of which most of its contents are  still a mystery to this day and are ripe  for all kinds of theories  from the magical like the holy grail and  the ark of the covenant to flat out  crazy alien illuminati conspiracy  theories to the more realistic stuff  like letters and leftovers from  historical figures it's definitely not  too far-fetched to think that the royal  family have these ancient objects stored  away somewhere  until misco ultimately managed to break  in and take off with some of it the  royal family has historically been  very serious about passing down and  preserving all kinds of magical  artifacts  stuff like the ocarina of time for  instance which kind of makes you think  do these vaults still reside in hyrule  castle right now if so  what else could be hidden there it's  unlikely that misco managed to clean up  the whole place right there have been  many speculations about the  disappearance of certain important  objects  like the aforementioned ocarina of time  for instance which isn't ever seen again  after the events of majora's mask  maybe link did eventually return it to  the royal family after his trip to  termina but just think about that for a  moment  the famous ocarina of time could be  right here hidden  somewhere within the walls of hyrule  castle right now if  only we could get to it but hey maybe  we'll find out more in a certain sequel  to breath of the wild  with all that said though one question  remains who  is or was misco the great bandit what  was his motivation and where is he now  is he long gone or is he still among us  somewhere  well there is the fact that his journal  just shows up and  no spoilers we will dive deeper into the  mystery of the great bandit himself over  on my channel masked nintendo bandit  yeah that seems fair right you are sir  so if you're interested in finding out  the identity of  misco the great bandit follow the link  in the description below to head on over  to the video that's already live over on  my channel  it also features your main man monster  maze of course you heard the man  anyway a big thanks to mass nintendo  bandit for joining me on this one  it's always fun working with you thanks  so much for having me man it's always a  pleasure to work together on videos  if you guys are interested in more zelda  theories or other kinds of nintendo  nonsense  head on over to my channel and check me  out this is masintonabanet signing out  and as always a big thanks to you for  watching and who could forget my  gracious patreon supporters and channel  members we got some new faces so say  hello to  jeff shepstone rachelan ipkiss mr  redbanana  thanks for joining on the minecraft live  stream by the way and andres monge  rodriquez  so sorry if i butchered your name and  that is all for today  i hope to see you in the next one we  have the next part of the evolution of  hyrule coming up soon  so join me then if you will this is dawn  signing off and  have a good one  [Music]  you

